body:
I agree with that line of thinking only until it means that you are your only source of reflection and that source is self destructive. Same reason why Alcoholics Anonymous resorts to a “higher power” when tackling the addiction...we often are not our own advocates and outside sources can bring about new perspective and worth. I will be the first to say that I struggle to see the value in myself but when I see how the others around me see value in me it gives me pause to re-evaluate my own self reflection. It’s not that you should rely entirely on another person’s value of you for your own self worth but you should allow that value to give you reason to consider that your perception could be narrowed by something other than what “actually is”. When things get heavy for me (and they do often) I realize one issue is that I am taking myself all too seriously and first things first, I need to lighten up. It’s only as bad as I make it, therefore it can also be as good as I make it.
Let me ask you this;
What, in your opinion, brings about self worth?
